      ],
      "hiddenInfo": "Brux, as the transitional layer between the bright wild and the deep dark, is where the corruption spreading through the Beastlands is hardest to see and easiest to spread, for in the eternal twilight the line between natural wariness and unnatural fear, between healthy shadow and creeping wrongness, is blurred by the gloaming itself. The madness poisoning Krigala's beasts passes through Brux on its way down and up, and the twilight layer's mist and shadow hide its movement; glades that have gone subtly wrong are far harder to spot in the dusk than in the noon. The twilight animal lords, creatures of the in-between hour, are uniquely suited to sensing what hides in shadow, and the spirit-fox — cleverest of all the animal lords — has begun to piece together what the bright-country lion could not: that the corruption is not a formless madness but a deliberate campaign, moving with intelligence, using the twilight layer as its highway between the day-world and the night-world. The fox has found the fiends' method: they are not attacking the beasts directly but poisoning the sacred springs and meres at which the beasts drink, so that the madness enters through the water and spreads wherever the water flows — which, in a plane threaded with springs and streams, is everywhere. The deeper secret the fox has not yet fully grasped is why Brux specifically matters to the enemy: the twilight layer is where the plane's transformation-magic is most fluid, where a beast can most easily be reshaped, and the fiends intend to use a corrupted twilight spring to breed something new and terrible — a beast that is not a beast, a predator with a fiend's mind wearing the sacred form of the wild, a wolf in truth as well as in the old saying. If such a thing were loosed in the dusk, it could move among the beast-souls unrecognized, spreading the madness by tooth and claw as well as by water.",
      "realm": "The Beastlands",
      "known": true
    },
    "Karasuthra": {
      "name": "Karasuthra",
      "basicInfo": "The third and deepest layer of the Beastlands, the realm of eternal night, a deep, dark, primal wilderness of night-black forests, moonlit plains, cavern-riddled mountains, and the great predatory dark, beneath a sky forever fixed at midnight and blazing with cold stars. Karasuthra is the nighttime face of the wild, the layer where the sun never rises and the deep, ancient, primal power of nature runs strongest and most dangerous: this is the country of the nocturnal beasts, the creatures of the true dark — the great wolves that run the moonlit plains, the hunting cats with their lamp-like eyes, the serpents in the shadowed grass, the owls and bats and all the beautiful predators of the night. The light of Karasuthra is starlight and moonlight, silver and cold and lovely, pooling in the clearings and glinting in a thousand watching eyes; the whole layer is wrapped in the electric, alive tension of the night-wild, where the hunt is constant and the balance of predator and prey is sharpest and most sacred. Its landscape is one of magnificent darkness: black old-growth forests where ancient things move unseen, silver plains where the great packs run beneath the moon, deep caverns where the night-things den, and high cold peaks under the blazing stars. It is the home of the nocturnal animal lords — the great spirit-wolf, the panther, the serpent, the owl of the deep night — the oldest and most powerful of all the animal lords, and of the petitioners who loved the night-wild and now hunt and run it in beast-form. Karasuthra has its deep gathering-dens where the night-beasts meet beneath the stars; its moonlit springs and hunting-grounds; its cavern-deeps and star-cold peaks; and the dark boundaries where the eternal night shades upward toward the twilight of Brux. It is the primal heart of the Beastlands, where the wild is most purely itself — beautiful, dangerous, and utterly untamed — and where the plane's fierce protective power runs deepest. Its dwellers are the mighty nocturnal animal lords, the night-loving petitioners, the celestial spirit-beasts of the dark, and the countless perfect predators and prey of the eternal, star-blazing night.",
