      "y": 2,
      "factions": [
        "The nocturnal animal lords (wolf, panther, serpent, night-owl)",
        "Beast-form petitioners of the night-wild",
        "Celestial spirit-beasts of the dark",
        "The Great Packs of Karasuthra",
        "The deep den-keepers and hunting-spirits"
      ],
      "hiddenInfo": "Karasuthra is where the corruption creeping down through the Beastlands means to make its final stand and its greatest triumph, for the deep night-layer is the primal heart of the plane, and to poison the wild here is to poison it at the root. The nocturnal animal lords are the oldest and mightiest of their kind, and the great spirit-wolf is the eldest and most powerful of all the animal lords in the plane — the true guardian of the Beastlands' deepest nature — which is precisely why the enemy covets Karasuthra: corrupt the deep night, turn the great predators, and the madness will flow up through twilight and noon to consume the whole plane from its heart outward. The fiendish incursion's ultimate target here is the Deepest Den, the primal source-place from which the spirit of the wild-hunt itself flows, where the sacred balance of predator and prey is most concentrated and most raw; a corruption introduced at the Deepest Den would not merely madden individual beasts but would twist the very principle of the hunt across the whole plane, turning the sacred predator-prey balance into an engine of endless, mindless slaughter — the wild's own life-force weaponized into pure carnage. The great spirit-wolf has felt the wrongness gathering in its deepest dens and has called the Great Packs to hunt the enemy through the night-country, and it alone among the animal lords has grasped the full shape of the threat: that the madness in Krigala, the poisoned springs of Brux, and the gathering dark in Karasuthra are one campaign, and that the enemy's goal is not conquest but corruption of the plane's very soul. But the wolf also knows the terrible danger of its own response, for to hunt the enemy through the deep night with the full fury of the Great Packs risks tipping the sacred balance toward exactly the mindless slaughter the enemy seeks to create — the wolf must destroy the corruption without becoming, in its fury, the very carnage it fights. And there is a final secret the wolf guards: the enemy has an agent already among the night-beasts, a fiend-minded predator bred in a corrupted twilight spring and loosed into Karasuthra wearing the sacred form of a great wolf, hidden within the very packs the spirit-wolf leads.",
      "realm": "The Beastlands",
      "known": true
    },
    "Arvandor": {
      "name": "Arvandor",
      "basicInfo": "The first and mightiest layer of Arborea, a realm of soaring snow-capped mountains, deep ancient forests, blossoming glades, rushing rivers, and blazing beauty, home to the elven gods of the Seldarine and the Greek Olympians, and the passionate, creative, heroic heart of the whole plane. Arvandor is Arborea at its most glorious: a landscape grander and more vividly alive than any mortal world, where the mountains rise impossibly high into skies of brilliant blue, the forests run deep and golden-green and alive with song, the glades blaze with impossible flowers, and every vista is composed like a masterpiece of art. This is the layer where beauty is worshipped and creation is sacred, where the elven gods keep their fabled realm of Arvandor-within-Arvandor amid the highest forests, where the Olympians feast and quarrel and love upon their mountain heights, and where the passionate good of the plane runs at its fullest flood. The souls who dwell here are the artists, lovers, heroes, and free spirits who lived with burning hearts — the elven petitioners who run the eternal forests, the poet-souls and singer-souls whose art never ends, the hero-souls who feast in the high halls, and the wild celestial spirits of beauty and passion. Arvandor has its sacred forests where the Seldarine walk; its Olympian heights where the Greek gods hold their court; its blazing glades of art and revelry where the endless feast and the endless song go on; its wild mountains and deep woods where beauty runs untamed; and its blossoming boundaries where the first layer meets the great ocean of Aquallor below. There are no ordered cities, only the glorious wild country and the passionate communities that gather in the fairest glades, and the whole layer breathes with creation, emotion, heroism, and fierce beauty. Its dwellers are the elven gods and Olympians, the artist and hero petitioners, the celestial spirits of passion and beauty, and the countless free souls living their afterlife at the full, burning intensity of a heart that never learned to hold back.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "factions": [
        "The Seldarine (elven gods of Arvandor)",
        "The Olympians (Greek gods of the heights)",
        "Artist, poet, and singer petitioners",
        "Hero-souls of the high feast-halls",
        "Wild celestial spirits of beauty and passion"
      ],
      "hiddenInfo": "Arvandor's glory is its passion, and its peril is that same passion carried to extremes, for the plane's fierce emotion — worshipped and unrestrained — can tip toward obsession, jealousy, and destructive excess, and something has begun to push it deliberately past its edge. A subtle corruption is spreading through the layer's emotional heart: artists whose creative passion has curdled into obsessive madness, unable to stop creating and destroying; lovers whose devotion has soured into jealous possession; heroes whose glory-lust has turned to reckless, ruinous violence. The passion that makes Arvandor the most vividly alive of all the Upper Planes is being weaponized against it, tipped grain by grain toward passion's own undoing. The suspected source is agents of the Abyss — for the demons understand that they cannot conquer Arborea's wild good by force, but they can corrupt it by inflaming its passions past the point where good can hold them, turning creation into obsession, love into jealousy, and heroism into slaughter, until the plane consumes itself in the very emotions that were its glory. The Seldarine and the Olympians, themselves beings of towering passion, are dangerously slow to recognize the threat, for the line between glorious passion and corrupted excess is precisely the line their whole plane walks, and they are prone to mistaking the early corruption for merely another burst of Arborean intensity. One elven demigod of the Seldarine, a patron of artists, has begun to notice that the maddened creators all drank from a particular wellspring of inspiration — a sacred spring of the muses whose waters were said to grant divine creativity — and suspects the enemy has poisoned inspiration itself at its source, so that the very thing that makes Arvandor's art divine now drives its artists to beautiful madness. The deeper danger is that the gods' own passions could be turned: if an Olympian or a member of the Seldarine were tipped into corrupted excess, the resulting divine obsession or jealousy could devastate the whole layer, for a god's passion is a god's power, and a god consumed by jealousy is a catastrophe with no easy remedy.",
      "realm": "Arborea",
      "known": true
    },
    "Aquallor": {
      "name": "Aquallor",
      "basicInfo": "The second layer of Arborea, the realm of the great infinite ocean, a boundless wine-dark sea of surpassing beauty beneath a sky of endless sunset-colors, where the sea-gods dwell, the deep passions run, and the water holds all the emotion of the plane distilled into its shining depths. Aquallor is Arborea's ocean-heart: after the soaring mountains and blazing forests of Arvandor, the plane descends into this vast, beautiful sea that stretches beyond all horizons, its waters running through every shade of wine-dark blue and sunset-gold, its surface scattered with fair islands and its depths holding wonders beyond telling. The sea of Aquallor is not merely water but the distilled emotion of the whole plane, and to sail or swim it is to feel the deep passions of Arborea washing through one's very soul — love and longing and grief and joy carried in the currents. This is the layer of the sea-gods and the deep-dwelling spirits, of the passions that run deep rather than blaze bright, of longing and memory and the beautiful sorrow that lies beneath all great joy. Its islands are fair and various — some blazing with their own smaller revelries, some quiet and contemplative, some sacred to particular sea-gods — and its depths are home to the celestial creatures of the deep and the drowned-soul petitioners who loved the sea. Aquallor has its shining island-havens where the sea-souls gather; its sacred sea-god shrines upon the fairest isles; its deep sanctuaries where the ocean's passions run deepest; its wine-dark currents that carry emotion through the whole layer; and its far horizons where the endless sea meets the sky and, at its lowest reaches, gives way to the white dust of Mithardir below. Its dwellers are the sea-gods and their courts, the ocean-loving petitioners, the celestial creatures of the deep, the island-communities of the passionate sea-souls, and the deep spirits of longing and memory — all wrapped in the beautiful, emotional, wine-dark vastness of the endless ocean.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1,
      "factions": [
        "The sea-gods and their courts",
        "Ocean-loving petitioners and drowned-souls",
        "Celestial creatures of the deep",
        "Island-communities of the passionate sea",
        "Deep spirits of longing and memory"
      ],
      "hiddenInfo": "Because the sea of Aquallor is the distilled emotion of the whole plane, it is uniquely vulnerable to the corruption spreading through Arborea: the poisoning of passion in Arvandor above flows down, quite literally, into these waters, and the wine-dark currents that carry emotion through the layer now carry the taint as well. The deep passions of Aquallor — longing, grief, the beautiful sorrow beneath all joy — are being twisted toward despair, and the sea-souls who dwell in the emotional depths feel it first: a longing that curdles into hopeless obsession, a grief that deepens into a drowning sorrow with no bottom, a beautiful melancholy tipping into true and dangerous darkness. The sea-gods, whose power runs with the tides of the plane's emotion, have begun to feel the corruption in their own domains, and the deepest danger is that the sea itself — being emotion made water — could become a sea of pure despair, drowning every soul that sails or swims it in a sorrow from which none could surface. There is a specific secret in the deep: at the lowest reach of Aquallor, where the wine-dark water gives way to the white dust of Mithardir, lies the Drowned Confluence, where the sea's distilled emotion pools most concentrated before it seeps down into the dead-god desert below — and the enemy has recognized that to corrupt the sea at this deepest point would poison not only Aquallor but would send tainted emotion seeping into Mithardir's fragile melancholy, potentially waking something in the desert of dead gods that should stay forgotten. One sea-god, a deity of longing and safe voyage, has begun gathering the deep spirits to guard the Drowned Confluence, but the corruption spreads through the emotional currents faster than any guard can be set, and the sea-god fears that the same enemy inflaming passion into obsession in Arvandor means to drown Aquallor in despair as the second movement of a single symphony of ruin.",
      "realm": "Arborea",
      "known": true
