      "difficultyTier": "2",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Ward of the Self-Condemned holds a soul who is not merely wracked by guilt but is being deliberately prevented from healing — a former cleric of Ilmater whose self-hatred is fed and sustained by a whispering agent of Loviatar, the Goddess of Pain, hidden among the recovering souls. Loviatar's servant works to turn Ilmater's own mercy against itself, keeping this soul in eternal torment as a slow experiment in whether the House of the Broken God can be made to fail even a single soul. If the healers cannot identify the whisperer, the failure could crack their faith in mercy's reach.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Well of Borne Sorrows": {
      "name": "The Well of Borne Sorrows",
      "basicInfo": "A sacred and terrible place at the center of Venya's highest terrace, a bottomless well into which Ilmater's most devoted martyrs pour the suffering they take from others, so that the pain of the multiverse might be safely contained rather than left to fester. The Well is the deepest expression of Ilmater's creed and its greatest burden: every anguish absorbed by his healers across uncounted ages is carried here and poured into the shaft, where it sinks away into a depth no soul has ever plumbed. The waters of the Well are black despite Venya's pearly light, for they hold concentrated agony distilled from the whole history of mortal suffering, and to gaze into them too long is to feel the weight of all the pain ever borne. The Well is watched at every hour by an order of martyr-keepers, for it must never overflow and never be shattered — were all the sorrow it holds to flood back into the multiverse at once, the resulting tide of anguish could break the will of every living being. It is at once the most merciful and most dangerous place in all of Venya.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Venya",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Terrace of Pouring": {
          "description": "The high terrace surrounding the Well's mouth, where the martyr-keepers come to pour the suffering they have gathered into the shaft. The terrace is austere and windswept, its pale stone stained faintly grey by ages of borne sorrow, and the martyrs move across it in slow procession, each bearing a vessel of absorbed anguish. The pouring is a solemn rite, performed in reverent silence, and the terrace is heavy with the weight of the mercy enacted here.",
          "paths": [
            "The Well's Mouth",
            "The Keeper's Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Well's Mouth": {
          "description": "The rim of the Well itself, a circle of black stone around a shaft that plunges into unfathomable depth. The waters far below glint blackly, and a cold that has nothing to do with temperature rises from the shaft — the chill of concentrated grief. Only the martyr-keepers may approach the very rim, and even they do so with care, for to lean too far and gaze into the depths is to risk being drawn down into the sorrow the Well holds. A low, wordless moaning rises faintly from far below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Pouring",
            "The Descent of the Deep Keepers"
          ]
        },
        "The Keeper's Vigil": {
          "description": "The watch-post where the order of martyr-keepers maintains its unbroken vigil over the Well. The keepers watch the level of the black water and the integrity of the shaft, ready to sound the alarm at the first sign of overflow or breach. Their leader, an ancient martyr named Brother Wound, has kept this vigil since the Well was first dug, and bears in his own broken form the memory of every sorrow ever poured into it. The vigil is the most solemn duty in all of Venya.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Pouring",
            "The Chamber of the Rising Level"
          ]
        },
        "The Descent of the Deep Keepers": {
          "description": "A perilous stair spiraling down the inside of the Well's shaft, walked only by the Deep Keepers — martyrs of such strength of spirit that they can descend partway into the concentrated sorrow to inspect the shaft's integrity and reinforce the ancient wards that contain it. The descent grows colder and heavier with each step, and the whispered griefs of ages press against the mind. Few keepers can descend far before they must turn back, and none has ever reached the bottom.",
          "paths": [
            "The Well's Mouth",
            "The Ward-Ring of Containment"
          ]
        },
        "The Ward-Ring of Containment": {
          "description": "A ring of ancient sigils carved into the shaft partway down, the great ward that keeps the Well's sorrow from rising back up and out. The Deep Keepers descend to this ring to renew the wards, tracing the sigils with tears of willing compassion — for only mercy freely given can hold back the tide of borne grief. The ring glows faintly in the dark of the shaft, and its slow, ages-long erosion is the keepers' deepest fear.",
          "paths": [
            "The Descent of the Deep Keepers"
          ]
        },
        "The Chamber of the Rising Level": {
          "description": "A recording-chamber beside the Vigil where the level of the Well's black water is measured and its slow rise over the ages is tracked. The chamber's records show a truth the keepers speak of only in hushed voices: the level rises faster than it once did, for the multiverse produces more sorrow than it once did, and the day may come when the Well can hold no more. Brother Wound studies these records with growing dread.",
          "paths": [
            "The Keeper's Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Grieving Garden": {
          "description": "A garden of grey and white flowers grown on the terrace below the Well, where the martyr-keepers rest and recover between their turns at the vigil and the descent. The flowers here are watered with ordinary tears rather than the concentrated sorrow of the Well, and tending them helps the keepers to bear the weight of their terrible duty. It is a quiet, melancholy place, but not a hopeless one, for even here the pale flowers bloom.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Pouring"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of the First Sorrow": {
          "description": "A memorial hall recording the very first sorrow ever poured into the Well — the grief that necessitated its digging — and the martyr who first chose to bear another's pain rather than let it fester in the world. The hall teaches new keepers why their duty exists and what it costs, and it holds the founding relics of their order. It is a place of grave initiation, where each new keeper first understands the true weight of the vigil they take up.",
          "paths": [
            "The Keeper's Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Overflow Channels": {
          "description": "A network of stone channels carved around the Well's mouth as a last defense, designed to catch and disperse any sorrow that might rise over the rim, draining it harmlessly into deep sinks lined with absorbing crystal. The channels have never been needed in all the Well's history, and the keepers pray they never will be, but they inspect them constantly, for they are the final barrier between the contained sorrow and the wider mountain should the Well ever truly overflow.",
          "paths": [
            "The Well's Mouth"
          ]
        },
        "The Sanctuary of the Untainted": {
          "description": "A warded refuge near the Well where a keeper whose spirit has been overwhelmed by the concentrated sorrow may retreat to be healed of the contamination before it takes root. Grief is contagious, and a keeper who bears too much for too long can be poisoned by it; the Sanctuary's gentle attendants draw the excess sorrow back out, restoring the keeper to wholeness. Without this refuge, the order of martyr-keepers could not endure their terrible work.",
          "paths": [
            "The Grieving Garden"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Martyr-Keepers of the Well",
        "The Deep Keepers",
        "Brother Wound's order",
        "Church of Ilmater (the Vigil)",
        "Ward-tracers of Containment"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "4",
      "hiddenInfo": "A cult of Loviatar has been secretly siphoning drops of the Well's black water through a hairline crack in the Ward-Ring of Containment, distilling the concentrated sorrow into a poison of pure despair that they intend to introduce into the water supplies of good-aligned cities in the living world. Each drop they steal weakens the ward-ring further, hastening the very overflow the keepers dread. Brother Wound has noticed the level dropping faster than the pouring accounts for, but cannot conceive that anyone would willingly steal such agony — which is exactly why the theft has gone undetected.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Refuge of the Weary": {
      "name": "The Refuge of the Weary",
      "basicInfo": "A great hospice-town on the pearly slopes of Venya, dedicated to sheltering and restoring the souls who arrive at this layer most exhausted by the long climb and the deep suffering of their mortal lives. The Refuge is Venya's answer to a hard truth: that the ascent of Mount Celestia, while ultimately joyful, is also arduous, and some souls reach the third layer worn nearly to nothing by grief, guilt, and the sheer effort of the climb. Here they may stop, sometimes for what feels like ages, and be cared for until they are ready to go on. The Refuge is a warm and welcoming place, a sprawling town of guest-houses, gardens, chapels, and quiet retreats, all devoted to the single purpose of restoring weary souls. It is staffed by the gentlest of Ilmater's petitioners and by souls who, having been restored here themselves, chose to stay and care for others in turn. No soul is ever turned away from the Refuge, and none is ever rushed onward before it is ready. It embodies Venya's deepest teaching: that mercy is not weakness but the truest strength, and that no one climbs the mountain alone.",
      "x": -15,
      "y": -41,
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Venya",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Welcoming Green": {
          "description": "A broad pearly meadow at the entrance to the Refuge where exhausted pilgrims are met by gentle petitioner-hosts and helped to their rest. The green is dotted with soft cushions and shaded arbors, and warm blessed snow falls softly over it. Here a soul at the end of its strength may simply lie down in the grass and be tended, asked for nothing, expected to do nothing, until it has gathered itself enough to speak of what it needs.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guest-Houses of Rest",
            "The Chapel of Small Mercies"
          ]
        },
        "The Guest-Houses of Rest": {
          "description": "A village of warm, comfortable guest-houses where weary souls dwell during their recovery, each tended by hosts who see to their every comfort. The houses are simple but deeply homely, and a soul may stay in one for as long as it needs, sometimes for what feels like whole mortal lifetimes. The hosts ask nothing in return but that their guests accept the care offered — which, for some deeply wounded souls, is itself the hardest thing.",
          "paths": [
            "The Welcoming Green",
            "The Baths of Easing",
            "The Quiet Cloister"
          ]
        },
        "The Chapel of Small Mercies": {
          "description": "A humble chapel dedicated to the small kindnesses that sustain the weary — a warm meal, a listening ear, a hand held in the dark. The chapel teaches that goodness is found not only in grand sacrifice but in the countless tiny mercies that carry a soul through its hardest hours. Pilgrims come here to give thanks for the small kindnesses shown them and to learn to offer such kindnesses in turn. It is one of the most beloved places in the Refuge.",
          "paths": [
            "The Welcoming Green"
          ]
        },
        "The Baths of Easing": {
          "description": "A series of warm pools fed by Venya's blessed streams, where weary souls soak away the aches of the long climb and the deeper aches of their mortal lives. The waters ease both body and spirit, and the baths are a place of quiet, communal comfort where recovering souls sometimes share the stories of their journeys. The gentle attendants tend the pools and offer soothing words to any soul who wishes to talk while it soaks.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guest-Houses of Rest"
          ]
        },
        "The Quiet Cloister": {
          "description": "A retreat of hushed cells and still gardens for souls who need silence and solitude to recover — those whose weariness is of a kind that company cannot ease. Here a soul may be entirely alone, undisturbed, for as long as it needs, with only the soft fall of warm snow and the distant murmur of the streams for company. The cloister's keepers check gently on each guest but otherwise leave them to their healing solitude.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guest-Houses of Rest",
            "The Garden of Returning Joy"
          ]
        },
        "The Kitchen of Comfort": {
          "description": "The warm heart of the Refuge, where simple, nourishing food is prepared for the weary souls — the plain, comforting meals that soothe a troubled spirit. The kitchen never closes, and any soul may come at any hour for a bowl of warm broth and a kind word. The cooks take special joy in learning each guest's favorite dish from their mortal life and preparing it as a gesture of welcome. It is astonishing how much healing begins with a familiar meal.",
          "paths": [
            "The Welcoming Green"
          ]
        },
        "The Garden of Returning Joy": {
          "description": "A garden of bright pearly flowers where recovering souls come as their spirits begin to mend, to feel the first returning stirrings of joy. The garden is deliberately cheerful, full of birdsong and gentle color, and its keepers watch with quiet delight as souls who arrived in despair begin, day by day, to smile again. It is the place where the Refuge's work most visibly bears fruit, and its keepers count each returning smile as a small victory.",
          "paths": [
            "The Quiet Cloister",
            "The Threshold of Renewed Climbing"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Shared Stories": {
          "description": "A warm communal hall where recovering souls who are ready gather to share the stories of their lives and their journeys, finding in the telling both healing for themselves and comfort for others who have suffered similarly. The hall is a place of laughter and tears, of hard tales bravely told and gently received. Many souls find that speaking their suffering aloud, among others who understand, is the final step in their recovery.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guest-Houses of Rest"
          ]
        },
        "The Threshold of Renewed Climbing": {
          "description": "The upper boundary of the Refuge, where restored souls gather to resume their ascent, renewed in body and spirit and ready for the higher, harder layers above. The threshold is a hopeful place, full of souls who arrived broken and now depart whole, and the hosts of the Refuge send each one onward with a blessing and the knowledge that they may always return if the climb proves too hard again. Many restored souls linger here a while, reluctant to leave the kindness that saved them.",
          "paths": [
            "The Garden of Returning Joy"
          ]
        },
        "The Memorial of Those Who Stayed": {
          "description": "A quiet shrine honoring the souls who, having been restored at the Refuge, chose to remain and care for others rather than continue their own ascent. Their sacrifice — to delay their own journey to the light in order to ease the journeys of others — is held in special honor here. Many of the Refuge's gentlest hosts are such souls, and the memorial reminds all who serve here of the noble tradition they carry forward.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Shared Stories"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "Petitioner-hosts of the Refuge",
        "Church of Ilmater (hospice order)",
        "The Restored-Who-Stayed",
        "Gentle attendants of the Baths",
        "Recovering pilgrims"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "1",
      "hiddenInfo": "One long-term guest in the Quiet Cloister is not a weary pilgrim but a spy — a soul that made a devil's bargain in life and was somehow permitted to ascend through a flaw in its judgment, now using the Refuge's no-questions-asked hospitality as a hiding place from which to observe the flow of vulnerable souls through Venya. It marks the most despairing and self-condemning guests and passes their names to the Loviataran cult, which targets them for corruption at their weakest moment. The Refuge's very virtue — that it asks nothing and turns no one away — is what the spy exploits.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Crystal Scriptorium": {
      "name": "The Crystal Scriptorium",
      "basicInfo": "The great library-city of Solania, a vast complex of luminous halls carved directly into the living crystal of the mountain, where the histories, laws, and deep truths of the multiverse are recorded and studied. The Scriptorium is the intellectual heart of Mount Celestia, a place where deva loremasters, archon scholars, and the wisest of the ascending souls labor to understand the principles of law and good that the whole plane embodies. Every wall glows with a soft electrum light drawn from the crystal itself, and the air hums faintly with the resonance of stored knowledge. Here the records of every great deed and terrible sin across the mortal worlds are inscribed into crystal tablets that never decay, and here the celestial powers come to consult the accumulated wisdom of ages when they face decisions that will shape the fate of planes. The Scriptorium is not a silent place; it rings with the murmur of debate and the scratch of styluses on crystal, for the pursuit of understanding is treated here as a form of worship. To be admitted to study in its deepest halls is one of the highest honors a soul can attain on the mountain, and some scholars remain here for what feels like ages, drawn ever deeper into the inexhaustible study of the good.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 6,
      "region": "Solania",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Electrum Atrium": {
          "description": "The grand entrance hall of the Scriptorium, a soaring space of pale gold-silver crystal where arriving scholars are received and oriented. The atrium's walls are inscribed with the founding principles of the library, and its light is the clear electrum glow that gives the whole layer its character. Deva greeters welcome new students and assess the questions that brought them, directing each to the halls where their inquiries may best be pursued.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Histories",
            "The Hall of Laws",
            "The Reading Cloisters"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Histories": {
          "description": "The vast archive where the histories of the mortal worlds are recorded in crystal tablets that never fade — every great deed, every terrible sin, every turning point in the long story of the struggle between good and evil. Deva historians labor ceaselessly to keep the records current, drawing on the reports of archons and the memories of the newly dead. Scholars come here to trace the deep patterns of history, and the powers of good consult these halls when they seek to understand how present dangers echo the perils of the past.",
          "paths": [
            "The Electrum Atrium",
            "The Vault of Sealed Records"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Laws": {
          "description": "The archive of principle, where the cosmic laws of good — the true, underlying rules by which righteousness operates — are studied and recorded. This is the most abstract and demanding hall in the Scriptorium, its crystal tablets inscribed with the deep philosophy of law and good that the archons live by. The tor archon jurists who preside here are the finest legal minds in the multiverse, and their rulings on questions of cosmic principle are sought by the good powers of every plane.",
          "paths": [
            "The Electrum Atrium",
            "The Chamber of First Principles"
          ]
        },
        "The Reading Cloisters": {
          "description": "A series of quiet study-alcoves carved into the crystal, where individual scholars pursue their inquiries in peaceful concentration. Each cloister glows with its own soft light, and the crystal walls seem to aid contemplation, clarifying the thoughts of those who study within. Scholars may reserve a cloister for what feels like ages, and some of the deepest insights in Celestia's long history have been achieved in these humble, luminous cells.",
          "paths": [
            "The Electrum Atrium",
            "The Scholar's Commons"
          ]
        },
        "The Vault of Sealed Records": {
          "description": "A guarded deep archive where the most dangerous knowledge is kept sealed away — the true names of bound fiends, the methods of terrible magics, the secrets whose telling would arm evil. The vault is warded and watched by sword archon guardians, and access to any sealed record requires the judgment of the tor archon conclave. It is a sober reminder that even in the pursuit of knowledge, some truths are too perilous to share freely.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Histories"
          ]
        },
        "The Chamber of First Principles": {
          "description": "The deepest hall of the Scriptorium, where the foundational truths of law and good are contemplated — the axioms from which all righteousness is derived. Only the most advanced scholars are admitted here, for the ideas contemplated in this chamber are so fundamental and so demanding that a lesser mind could be overwhelmed by them. The tor archon philosophers who dwell here are among the wisest beings in the multiverse, and their contemplations shape the very nature of good on the plane.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Laws",
            "The Resonance Deep"
          ]
        },
        "The Scholar's Commons": {
          "description": "A warm communal hall where the scholars of the Scriptorium gather to debate, share discoveries, and rest from their studies. The commons rings with vigorous, good-natured argument, for the pursuit of truth here is a joyful, collaborative endeavor. Scholars of every celestial race and every mortal origin mingle freely, and many a great insight has been sparked by a chance conversation over a shared meal in these lively halls.",
          "paths": [
            "The Reading Cloisters"
          ]
        },
        "The Crystal Presses": {
          "description": "The workshops where new knowledge is inscribed into the everlasting crystal tablets, using styluses of blessed metal that etch light itself into the stone. The presses are tended by skilled petitioner-scribes who take great care with every inscription, for a record made here will endure for as long as the mountain stands. The rhythmic scratch and soft chime of inscription fills these halls, the sound of knowledge being made permanent.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Histories"
          ]
        },
        "The Resonance Deep": {
          "description": "A profound chamber at the very heart of the Scriptorium where the accumulated knowledge of the whole library resonates through the crystal, and a scholar who sits in perfect stillness may hear echoes of truths not yet consciously known. It is a place of intuition and revelation, where the deepest understanding comes not from reading but from listening to the harmonics of the crystal itself. Few scholars are attuned enough to benefit from the Resonance Deep, but those who are have achieved wisdom found nowhere else.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chamber of First Principles"
          ]
        },
        "The Cartographer's Hall": {
          "description": "A specialized archive devoted to the mapping of the planes themselves — the shifting geographies of the multiverse, the pathways between worlds, the locations of hidden and sacred places. Deva cartographers labor to keep the great planar maps current, an endless task given the fluid nature of many planes. The powers of good consult these maps when they plan their movements against the forces of evil, and the hall is thus one of the more strategically vital in the Scriptorium.",
          "paths": [
            "The Scholar's Commons"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Unfinished Questions": {
          "description": "A gallery devoted to the great questions that remain unanswered even after ages of study — the deepest mysteries of good, evil, free will, and the nature of the multiverse. Each unanswered question is inscribed on a crystal pillar, and scholars add their contributions to the ongoing contemplation of each across the ages. The hall is a humbling place, a monument to the limits of even celestial understanding, and a spur to the endless pursuit of deeper truth.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chamber of First Principles"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "Deva Loremasters",
        "Tor Archon jurists and philosophers",
        "Petitioner-scribes",
        "Church of Oghma (celestial annex)",
        "Visiting scholars of the good powers"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "2",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Vault of Sealed Records has been subtly infiltrated — not by a fiend, but by a modron emissary from Mechanus operating with the quiet cooperation of a single tor archon jurist who has come to believe that Celestia's goodness would be perfected by pure order. Together they are copying the Hall of Laws' deepest principles, seeking the theoretical basis by which free will itself might be 'corrected' into lawful inevitability. This scholarly conspiracy is the intellectual arm of the same modron incursion tunneling toward the Vein of First Law, and it is far more dangerous, for it works not with drills but with ideas.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Prism Sanctum": {
      "name": "The Prism Sanctum",
      "basicInfo": "A sacred crystalline temple at the heart of Solania where the pure light descending from the summit is studied, refracted, and understood — the place where the celestial scholars come closest to comprehending the nature of the ultimate good that pours down from Chronias far above. The Prism Sanctum is Solania's most sacred site, a temple built around a great natural prism of flawless crystal through which the summit's light passes, splitting into its component virtues so that the scholars may study each in turn. Where the summit's light is too pure and overwhelming to be comprehended directly, here it is gently refracted into understandable components — the light of justice, the light of mercy, the light of courage, and all the other facets of the good — so that celestial minds may contemplate them one by one. The Sanctum is a place of profound reverence and deep study, where the theology of the good is pursued at its highest level, and where the scholars strive to understand what awaits at the summit of the mountain. It is also a place of great beauty, for the refracted light fills the temple with shifting rainbows of pure virtue, and to stand within it is to be bathed in the very components of goodness itself.",
      "x": 13,
      "y": -8,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Solania",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Refracting Nave": {
          "description": "The great central hall of the Sanctum, where the summit's light passes through the flawless crystal prism and splits into its component virtues, filling the nave with shifting rainbows of pure goodness. Scholars gather here to contemplate the refracted light, each drawn to the facet of virtue they most seek to understand. The nave is a place of overwhelming beauty and reverence, and simply standing within its shifting light is said to strengthen the corresponding virtues in the soul of the beholder.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chapel of Justice's Light",
            "The Chapel of Mercy's Light",
            "The Prism Chamber"
          ]
        },
        "The Prism Chamber": {
          "description": "The inner sanctum housing the great prism itself, a flawless crystal through which the summit's light descends and divides. The prism is the most sacred object in Solania, and it is tended by a small order of deva keepers who ensure its perfect clarity, for the slightest flaw would distort the light of the good. Access to the prism chamber is restricted to these keepers and to scholars of the highest attainment, for the concentrated light here is powerful enough to overwhelm an unprepared spirit.",
          "paths": [
            "The Refracting Nave",
            "The Ascending Light Shaft"
          ]
        },
        "The Chapel of Justice's Light": {
          "description": "A chapel bathed in the refracted light of justice, where scholars and pilgrims contemplate the nature of righteous judgment. The light here is clear and unwavering, and those who meditate within it find their sense of justice sharpened and their understanding of fairness deepened. Justiciars from the Tor of Judgment sometimes come here to renew their commitment to true justice before rendering their hardest verdicts.",
          "paths": [
            "The Refracting Nave"
          ]
        },
        "The Chapel of Mercy's Light": {
          "description": "A chapel bathed in the refracted light of mercy, where the followers of Ilmater and all who seek to understand compassion come to contemplate. The light here is warm and gentle, and those who meditate within it find their capacity for mercy deepened. The chapel stands in deliberate proximity to the Chapel of Justice's Light, for the scholars teach that justice and mercy must always be studied together, each incomplete without the other.",
          "paths": [
            "The Refracting Nave"
          ]
        },
        "The Ascending Light Shaft": {
          "description": "A vertical shaft rising from the Prism Chamber toward the higher layers, through which the summit's light descends into the Sanctum. Looking up the shaft, one sees the light growing purer and more overwhelming toward its distant source, a glimpse of the ineffable radiance that awaits at the summit. Scholars gaze up the shaft in contemplation of the ultimate good, though none can look for long, for the light grows too pure to bear the higher one's gaze travels.",
          "paths": [
            "The Prism Chamber"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Studied Virtues": {
          "description": "An archive where the scholars record their contemplations of the refracted virtues, building an ever-deepening theology of the good. Each facet of virtue revealed by the prism is studied, debated, and documented here, and the accumulated understanding forms the highest theology available to celestial minds. The hall is a place of profound scholarship, where the very nature of goodness is pursued with rigorous devotion.",
          "paths": [
            "The Refracting Nave"
          ]
        },
        "The Meditation Prisms": {
          "description": "A gallery of smaller prisms where individual scholars may study a single refracted virtue in solitary contemplation, each prism casting the light of one facet of goodness into a private meditation cell. The scholars sit within the colored light for what feels like ages, seeking to understand and embody the virtue it represents. It is said that a scholar who truly comprehends even one facet of the good through these prisms is forever changed by the understanding.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Studied Virtues"
          ]
        },
        "The Keeper's Cloister": {
          "description": "The dwelling of the deva keepers who tend the great prism and maintain its perfect clarity. Their devotion to the prism is total, for they understand that the whole Sanctum's purpose depends on the flawlessness of the crystal they guard. The cloister is austere and reverent, and the keepers speak little, their whole existence given to the sacred task of keeping the light of the good undistorted.",
          "paths": [
            "The Prism Chamber"
          ]
        },
        "The Spectrum Garden": {
          "description": "A garden where luminous flowers bloom in every color of the refracted light, each species corresponding to a facet of virtue, cultivated as a living study of the good made manifest in growing things. The garden is a place of beauty and contemplation, where scholars walk among the virtue-flowers to refresh their understanding. The flowers of justice grow beside the flowers of mercy, the flowers of courage beside the flowers of humility, a living illustration of the harmony of the virtues.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Studied Virtues"
          ]
        },
        "The Threshold of Unbearable Light": {
          "description": "The upper boundary of the Sanctum, where the light shaft rises toward Mertion and the higher layers, and where the refracted, bearable light of the Sanctum gives way to the purer, harder radiance above. Scholars who have completed their studies here pass through this threshold to continue their ascent toward the platinum light of Mertion, carrying with them a deepened understanding of the virtues they have contemplated. It is a place of transition from study toward the proving that awaits above.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ascending Light Shaft"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
