      ],
      "difficultyTier": "2",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Chamber of Impossible Weighings has begun to fill with souls that cannot be weighed at all — not because they are ambiguous, but because the lesser scales, attuned to the cracking Unblinking Scale, are beginning to give false and contradictory measurements. Souls of genuine righteousness are being turned back while subtler flaws pass unnoticed, and the weighers, trusting their instruments, do not realize their scales are failing. If the Unblinking Scale shatters, every weighing on this terrace will become meaningless, and the whole just order of the ascent — the honest measurement that lets souls know their true progress — will collapse into chaos.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Heart of Celestia": {
      "name": "The Heart of Celestia",
      "basicInfo": "The great ruby fortress at the center of Jovar, within which burns the light that illuminates all seven layers of the sacred mountain, and whose true and secret function is to filter the raw, identity-dissolving radiance of the summit into a light that lower beings can survive. The Heart of Celestia is the most vital structure on the entire mountain, for without it the unfiltered light of Chronias would pour down the slopes and dissolve every soul, archon, and god upon them into the anonymous perfection of the summit. It rises from Jovar's blazing terraces as a fortress cut from a single colossal ruby, its walls glowing from within with the stepped-down light of the ultimate good, and it is guarded by the Empyreal Guard, the mightiest archons in all of Celestia, whose secret duty is not to keep enemies out but to keep the summit's light in. Within the Heart, the light of Chronias descends through a series of great filtering chambers, each softening the radiance further, until it emerges as the bearable, holy light that warms the whole mountain. To stand within the Heart is to be as close to the ultimate good as any being can come while still remaining oneself, and the archons who serve here carry the awesome weight of maintaining the balance on which all of Celestia depends.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 6,
      "region": "Jovar",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Ruby Gate": {
          "description": "The great entrance to the Heart, a portal cut from flawless ruby that glows with the stepped-down light of the summit. The gate is guarded by the mightiest of the Empyreal Guard, and it opens only to those of the highest perfection, for the light within grows purer than any lesser being could bear. To pass through the Ruby Gate is to enter the most sacred and most vital structure on the whole mountain, and even the greatest archons approach it with reverence.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Descending Light",
            "The Guard's Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Descending Light": {
          "description": "The great central hall of the Heart, through which the light of Chronias descends from the summit above, growing more bearable as it passes downward through the fortress. The hall blazes with a radiance almost too pure to endure, and the archons who tend it are among the few beings who can bear its light. Here the raw good of the summit begins its transformation into the light that warms the mountain, and the hall thrums with the awesome power of the ultimate good passing through.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ruby Gate",
            "The First Filtering Chamber",
            "The Choir Gallery"
          ]
        },
        "The First Filtering Chamber": {
          "description": "The first of the great chambers through which the summit's light is stepped down toward bearability, where the most concentrated radiance is gently diffused through veils of blessed crystal. The light here is still nearly overwhelming, and only the Empyreal Guard and the highest keepers may enter. The filtering is a delicate and vital process, for too much filtering would dim the mountain's holiness and too little would let the dissolving light through, and the keepers maintain the balance with infinite care.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Descending Light",
            "The Deep Filtering Chambers"
          ]
        },
        "The Guard's Vigil": {
          "description": "The watch-post of the Empyreal Guard, from which the mightiest archons in Celestia keep their secret and awesome vigil over the Heart. Their true duty, known to few, is not to repel invaders but to ensure that the summit's light never escapes unfiltered, for a single breach in the Heart's function would doom the whole mountain. The Guard are beings of tremendous power and gravity, and their vigil is the most consequential in all of Celestia, though its true nature is one of the plane's deepest secrets.",
          "paths": [
            "The Ruby Gate",
            "The Chamber of the Filtered Flame"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Filtering Chambers": {
          "description": "The series of inner chambers through which the summit's light passes on its long journey toward bearability, each softening the radiance further until it emerges as the holy light that warms the mountain. The deep chambers are tended by keepers of surpassing perfection, for the light within grows purer the deeper one goes, approaching the raw radiance of Chronias itself. The chambers are the true engine of the Heart, and their perfect functioning sustains all of Celestia.",
          "paths": [
            "The First Filtering Chamber",
            "The Threshold of Raw Radiance"
          ]
        },
        "The Choir Gallery": {
          "description": "A gallery where the archdeva choir sings the hymns that harmonize the filtering of the light, for the stepping-down of the summit's radiance is not merely a mechanical process but a sacred harmony that requires the perfect song of the choir. The gallery rings with music of transcendent beauty, and the choir's endless hymn is one of the forces that keeps the Heart in balance. To hear the choir sing within the Heart is said to be the closest a soul can come to hearing the voice of the ultimate good itself.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Descending Light",
            "The Conductor's Sanctum"
          ]
        },
        "The Chamber of the Filtered Flame": {
          "description": "The chamber where the fully stepped-down light of the summit gathers before it is sent forth to illuminate the whole mountain — the source of the holy radiance that warms every layer from Jovar down to Lunia's silver sea. The filtered flame burns here with a warm, bearable, glorious light, the very essence of Celestia's holiness made manageable for its inhabitants. From this chamber the light flows outward and downward, and its steady burning is the visible sign that the Heart's vital function continues unbroken.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guard's Vigil",
            "The Distribution Nexus"
          ]
        },
        "The Threshold of Raw Radiance": {
          "description": "The deepest and most perilous point in the Heart, where the unfiltered light of Chronias first enters the fortress from the summit above, before any stepping-down has occurred. The radiance here is the raw, identity-dissolving light of the ultimate good, and no being can approach it without risking dissolution into the summit's oneness. Only a single keeper of the very highest perfection maintains the vigil at this threshold, and their service is the most dangerous and most sacred duty in all of Celestia.",
          "paths": [
            "The Deep Filtering Chambers"
          ]
        },
        "The Conductor's Sanctum": {
          "description": "The sanctum of the archdeva who conducts the choir and oversees the harmonic filtering of the light, one of the most perfected beings on the whole mountain. The conductor holds the awesome responsibility of maintaining the sacred harmony on which the Heart's function partly depends, and their sanctum radiates a serene mastery of the ultimate good. Only the highest servants of the celestial powers may enter, and the conductor's work is among the most vital and least understood on the plane.",
          "paths": [
            "The Choir Gallery"
          ]
        },
        "The Distribution Nexus": {
          "description": "The point from which the filtered light of the summit is sent forth to illuminate all seven layers of the mountain, a nexus of radiant channels that carry the holy light outward and downward to every corner of Celestia. The nexus is a marvel of sacred engineering, ensuring that each layer receives exactly the light it needs, and its keepers monitor the flow with vigilant care. From here the light that gives Celestia its holiness begins its journey to the furthest reaches of the plane.",
          "paths": [
            "The Chamber of the Filtered Flame"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Empyreal Guard",
        "Keepers of the Ruby Heart",
        "The Archdeva Choir",
        "The Conductor's order",
        "Keepers of the Filtering Chambers"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "5",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Empyreal Guard's secret duty — keeping the summit's light in rather than keeping enemies out — is known to only a handful of beings on the mountain, and it conceals a terrible vulnerability: the Heart could be sabotaged not by breaking in, but by disrupting its filtering so that the raw radiance of Chronias pours down the mountain and dissolves everything into anonymous perfection. The forces of Hell have never understood the Heart's true function and so have never targeted it correctly. But the modron incursion rising through Solania and Mertion has grasped it exactly: the modrons calculate that the summit's unfiltered light, which dissolves all individuality, is itself a kind of ultimate 'order,' and a radical faction intends to shatter the Heart's filters and let Chronias consume the mountain — reasoning that a Celestia dissolved into perfect, undifferentiated oneness is more orderly than one full of distinct, free-willed souls.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Choir of the Ascended": {
      "name": "The Choir of the Ascended",
      "basicInfo": "The great singing-city of Jovar, where the archdeva choir and the most perfected of the ascended souls join in the eternal hymn that fills the sixth layer with transcendent music and helps to harmonize the sacred light of the Heart. The Choir of the Ascended is a place of pure, overwhelming beauty, where music is worship and worship is music, and where the voices of the most perfected beings on the mountain blend into a hymn so glorious that it is said to carry the prayers of all Celestia upward toward the summit. The city is built as a vast concert of radiant halls and resonant galleries, each attuned to a different part of the eternal hymn, and the whole rings ceaselessly with music of transcendent power. The choir's song is not merely beautiful; it is functional, for the sacred harmony it produces helps to maintain the filtering of the summit's light in the Heart of Celestia, and thus the singers of Jovar are, in their way, as vital to the mountain's survival as the Empyreal Guard themselves. To hear the Choir of the Ascended is to experience the closest thing to the voice of the ultimate good that any soul can bear, and pilgrims who reach this height are often moved beyond words by the glory of the eternal hymn.",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 6,
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Jovar",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Great Concert Hall": {
          "description": "The vast central hall of the Choir, where the full archdeva choir and the most perfected ascended souls join in the eternal hymn. The hall is designed for perfect acoustics, and the music that fills it is of a beauty and power beyond mortal comprehension. To stand within the Great Concert Hall while the full choir sings is said to be the most transcendent experience available to any soul short of the summit itself, and pilgrims are often overwhelmed by the glory of the hymn.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gallery of Harmonies",
            "The Singer's Sanctum",
            "The Resonant Nave"
          ]
        },
        "The Gallery of Harmonies": {
          "description": "A gallery of resonant chambers, each attuned to a different part of the eternal hymn, where individual sections of the choir practice and perfect their portions of the sacred music. The harmonies produced here blend into the whole hymn that fills the layer, and each chamber rings with its own part of the transcendent music. The gallery is a marvel of sacred acoustics, and the perfected singers who dwell here have honed their voices over ages to a perfection beyond mortal reach.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Concert Hall",
            "The Chamber of New Voices"
          ]
        },
        "The Singer's Sanctum": {
          "description": "The dwelling of the archdeva singers who lead the eternal choir, beings whose voices are so perfected that they can bear a part in the harmony that sustains the Heart's filtering. The singers dwell in serene devotion to their sacred music, and their sanctum radiates the peace of those who have found their purpose in the highest worship. Their voices are among the most vital forces on the mountain, for the harmony they produce helps to keep the summit's light in balance.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Concert Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Resonant Nave": {
          "description": "A great nave where the choir's hymn resonates most powerfully, its architecture designed to amplify and harmonize the sacred music until it seems to fill the whole of creation. The nave is a place of overwhelming musical glory, and the resonance here is so pure that it is said to carry the prayers of all Celestia upward toward the summit. Pilgrims who enter the Resonant Nave during the full hymn are often moved to tears by the transcendent beauty of the music.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Concert Hall",
            "The Ascending Harmony"
          ]
        },
        "The Chamber of New Voices": {
          "description": "A chamber where souls who have newly ascended to Jovar are taught to add their voices to the eternal hymn, learning the sacred music that they will sing for ages to come. The teaching is gentle and joyful, for to join the Choir of the Ascended is one of the highest honors on the mountain, and the new voices are welcomed with delight. The chamber rings with the earnest practice of souls learning to sing the highest worship of the good.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gallery of Harmonies"
          ]
        },
        "The Conductor's Rise": {
          "description": "A high platform from which the master conductor of the Choir directs the eternal hymn, coordinating the vast choir into a single perfect harmony. The conductor is one of the most perfected beings on the mountain, for the task of harmonizing the whole choir requires a mastery of the sacred music that few can attain. From the Conductor's Rise, the whole glorious concert of Jovar is directed, and the conductor's work helps to sustain the balance of the Heart itself.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Concert Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Silent Contemplation": {
          "description": "A hall of perfect silence amid the ceaseless music, where singers withdraw to rest their voices and contemplate the meaning of the hymn they sing. The silence here is as profound as the music is glorious, and the contrast reminds the singers of the sacred purpose of their song. Singers come here between their turns in the choir to restore their spirits and deepen their understanding of the worship they offer, for even the most perfected voice needs rest and reflection.",
          "paths": [
            "The Singer's Sanctum"
          ]
        },
        "The Gallery of Ancient Hymns": {
          "description": "An archive where the sacred hymns of the choir are preserved — the great songs of worship that have filled Jovar since the plane's creation. The hymns are recorded in a notation of light, and the keepers of the gallery preserve the whole tradition of the choir's sacred music. Singers come here to study the ancient hymns and to draw on the accumulated musical wisdom of ages, and the gallery is a treasury of the highest worship of the good.",
          "paths": [
            "The Gallery of Harmonies"
          ]
        },
        "The Ascending Harmony": {
          "description": "The point where the choir's hymn rises toward the summit, carrying the worship of all Celestia upward toward the ultimate good of Chronias. The harmony here is at its most pure and powerful, and the music seems almost to become light as it ascends toward the summit. It is the culmination of the choir's sacred purpose, the point where their eternal hymn passes beyond the reach of any soul that has not made the final ascent, offered up to the ultimate good itself.",
          "paths": [
            "The Resonant Nave"
          ]
        },
        "The Garden of Singing Flowers": {
          "description": "A garden where luminous flowers ring with soft music in the ruby light of Jovar, their gentle chimes blending with the choir's eternal hymn. The garden is a place of delicate beauty, where the singers walk to refresh their spirits amid the music of growing things. The singing flowers are said to have grown from the seeds of especially beautiful hymns, and their music is a small, sweet echo of the great choir that fills the layer.",
          "paths": [
            "The Hall of Silent Contemplation"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Archdeva Choir",
        "The Master Conductor's order",
        "The Ascended Singers",
        "Keepers of Ancient Hymns",
        "Teachers of New Voices"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "3",
      "hiddenInfo": "The eternal hymn of the Choir is one of the hidden forces that maintains the filtering of the summit's light in the Heart of Celestia — a fact known to the conductor but few others. This means the Choir is a second, unguarded vulnerability: if the eternal hymn were ever disrupted, silenced, or thrown into discord, the Heart's filtering would falter even without any direct attack on the fortress itself. The modron faction plotting to shatter the Heart has begun to understand this, and has considered introducing a subtle dissonance into the Choir — a single voice singing a mathematically 'perfect' but soulless harmony that would gradually pull the whole hymn toward a cold, dissolving order, unraveling the sacred music from within.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Threshold of the Summit": {
      "name": "The Threshold of the Summit",
      "basicInfo": "The highest place on the mountain that a soul may reach and still remain itself, the sacred boundary-region of Jovar where the final ascent to Chronias begins and where the most perfected beings prepare to surrender their individuality into the ultimate oneness of the good. The Threshold of the Summit is a place of profound and holy transition, the last waystation before the deepest mystery of the mountain, where those who have completed their long climb gather to make the final, irreversible ascent. Here the light of Chronias grows so pure that it can barely be borne, and the beings who dwell here — keepers, guides, and those preparing for the final ascent — are among the most perfected on the whole mountain. The Threshold is not a place of ordinary geography, for it stands at the very edge of the summit's identity-dissolving radiance, and its halls and terraces seem to shimmer at the boundary between form and formlessness. It is watched over by the Unnamed Watchers, mysterious beings who guard the final threshold and guide the most perfected souls toward their ultimate ascent. To reach the Threshold of the Summit is to stand at the very culmination of the mountain's long journey, one step away from becoming one with the light itself, and the region is suffused with an awe and a holiness beyond anything on the lower layers.",
      "x": 10,
      "y": -10,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Jovar",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Last Waystation": {
          "description": "The final resting-place before the ascent to the summit, where the most perfected beings gather to prepare for their surrender into the ultimate oneness of Chronias. The waystation is a place of profound peace and holy anticipation, for those who reach it have completed their long climb and stand at the very threshold of their ultimate reward. The guides here help each soul prepare for the final, irreversible ascent, and the waystation is suffused with the awe of the deepest mystery approaching.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Final Preparation",
            "The Watchers' Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Terrace of Final Preparation": {
          "description": "A terrace at the very edge of the summit's radiance, where the most perfected beings make their final preparations to ascend, contemplating the surrender of individuality that the final ascent requires. The light here is almost too pure to bear, and those who gather on the terrace are on the very threshold of becoming one with the ultimate good. It is a place of holy trepidation and profound peace, where the last traces of self are gently prepared for their dissolution into the light.",
          "paths": [
            "The Last Waystation",
            "The Ascending Path of No Return"
          ]
        },
        "The Watchers' Vigil": {
          "description": "The watch-post of the Unnamed Watchers, the mysterious beings who guard the final threshold of the mountain and guide the most perfected souls toward their ultimate ascent. The Watchers are among the most enigmatic beings in all of Celestia, their nature and origin unknown even to the archons, and their vigil at the threshold of the summit is one of the deepest mysteries of the plane. They neither prevent nor compel the final ascent, but they ensure that only those truly ready approach the summit's dissolving light.",
          "paths": [
            "The Last Waystation",
            "The Chamber of the Shadow-Flaw"
          ]
        },
        "The Ascending Path of No Return": {
          "description": "The final path from the Threshold into the summit of Chronias, walked only by those ready to surrender their individuality into the ultimate oneness of the good. Those who walk this path do not return, for they pass into the summit and become one with the light itself, their long journey up the mountain finally complete. It is the last threshold, the end of all ascent, and the most sacred passage in all of Celestia, suffused with a holiness beyond words.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Final Preparation"
          ]
        },
        "The Hall of Last Farewells": {
          "description": "A hall where those about to make the final ascent may take their leave of the companions and loved ones they have journeyed with, before passing into the oneness of the summit where individual bonds dissolve into universal love. The farewells here are bittersweet, for the ascent is both the ultimate reward and the end of the individual self that could love particular others. The hall is a place of tender partings and profound hope, at the very threshold of the deepest mystery.",
          "paths": [
            "The Last Waystation"
          ]
        },
        "The Chamber of the Shadow-Flaw": {
          "description": "A guarded and secret chamber near the very threshold of the summit, where the Unnamed Watchers keep their closest vigil over the single point of shadow that persists within Chronias — the flaw at the heart of perfect light. This is the closest any being may safely come to the summit's one imperfection, the doorway created by a soul that refused to surrender its identity out of love. The Watchers guard this chamber with a gravity beyond any other duty on the mountain, for the shadow-flaw is the one point where the perfect isolation of the summit might be breached.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watchers' Vigil"
          ]
        },
        "The Terrace of Contemplated Oneness": {
          "description": "A terrace where the most perfected beings contemplate the nature of the oneness they are about to enter, wrestling with the profound mystery of surrendering the self into the ultimate good. The contemplation here is the deepest available to any being that still retains its individuality, for it concerns the very meaning of the dissolution that awaits at the summit. Those who contemplate here approach an understanding of the ultimate good that no lesser soul can attain.",
          "paths": [
            "The Terrace of Final Preparation"
          ]
        },
        "The Shrine of the Completed Journey": {
          "description": "A shrine honoring the completion of the mountain's long ascent, dedicated to the truth that every soul's climb, however long and hard, leads at last to this threshold and the ultimate good beyond. The shrine is a place of profound gratitude and fulfillment, where those about to ascend give thanks for the journey that brought them here. It celebrates the deepest promise of the mountain: that the long climb toward the good is always, ultimately, completed.",
          "paths": [
            "The Last Waystation"
          ]
        },
        "The Watcher's Sanctum": {
          "description": "The innermost dwelling of the Unnamed Watchers, a place of deep mystery that no other being has ever entered. The nature of the Watchers and their sanctum is unknown even to the highest archons, and speculation about their origin is one of the enduring mysteries of Celestia. Whatever the Watchers are, their vigil at the threshold of the summit — and especially over the shadow-flaw — is among the most vital and enigmatic services on the whole mountain.",
          "paths": [
            "The Watchers' Vigil"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Unnamed Watchers",
        "Guides of the Final Ascent",
        "The Near-Perfected preparing to ascend",
        "Keepers of the Threshold"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "5",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Unnamed Watchers guard the Chamber of the Shadow-Flaw because it is the one point in all the multiverse where something could pass back down from the ultimate good of Chronias into the lower planes — a doorway that the summit's own perfection cannot close, created by a single soul's loving refusal to dissolve. The Watchers know that both the deepest fiends and the modron faction covet this doorway: the fiends because passing through it in reverse might let something touch or corrupt the ultimate good itself, and the modrons because they believe the shadow-flaw could be 'corrected' — the last free choice in a realm of perfect oneness, eliminated to make even Chronias fully lawful. The Watchers' true nature is the mountain's deepest secret, but their purpose is singular: to ensure that the one imperfection born of love is never exploited by those who would use it to unmake the good.",
      "known": true
    },
    "Glitterhearth": {
      "name": "Glitterhearth",
      "basicInfo": "The great market-town at the heart of Dothion, a cheerful, bustling hub where the produce of a thousand farms, the wares of a thousand workshops, and the folk of a hundred villages all come together in one glorious crossroads of honest trade and good living. Glitterhearth is not a city of ambition but a town of abundance, sprawling comfortably around a wide central green where market-stalls crowd beneath striped awnings and the air rings with haggling, laughter, hammering, and song. It is the place a visitor to Dothion should come first, for it samples the whole of the cultivated paradise in one walkable place: here are the craft-guilds and their workshops, the farmers' market and the grain-halls, the breweries and bake-houses, the gnome inventors' cluttered ateliers, the halfling family inns, the shrines to Garl Glittergold and Yondalla, and — descending from a great trapdoor-hall on the green — the topmost entrances to the deep gnome tunnels that honeycomb the earth below. Named for the warm forge-glow and the glitter of gnomish gems that light its evenings, Glitterhearth is a town where no one is a stranger for long, where every craft is practiced and every good thing traded, and where the ordinary joys of Dothion — good work, good food, good company — are concentrated into one endlessly welcoming whole. It serves as the natural gateway to everything Dothion offers, and from its roads a traveler may set out to any farm, village, workshop, or mountain-crossing in the cultivated world.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 7,
      "region": "Dothion",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Market Green": {
          "description": "The wide central square of Glitterhearth, crowded with market-stalls beneath striped awnings where farmers, craftsfolk, and traders from across Dothion sell their goods in cheerful, bustling abundance. Every honest ware of the cultivated paradise can be found here: heaped produce from the never-failing farms, gnomish contraptions that whir and chime, halfling pies and preserves, bolts of woven cloth, gleaming tools and pots. The green rings with haggling and laughter, and no visitor to Dothion sees its true heart until they have wandered these crowded, joyful rows. A great old bell hangs at the center to call the town to feast, alarm, or celebration.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guild Row",
            "The Farmers' Grain-Halls",
            "The Trapdoor Hall",
            "The Welcoming Inns"
          ]
        },
        "The Guild Row": {
          "description": "A street of craft-guild halls and workshops where the smiths, weavers, potters, carpenters, and other artisans of Dothion practice and perfect their trades and pass their skills to eager apprentices. Each hall rings with the sounds of its craft — the ping of hammers, the clack of looms, the whir of potters' wheels — and the doors stand open so passersby may watch the masters at work. The guilds of Glitterhearth are famed across Dothion, and to earn a place among them is a petitioner's proudest achievement. Skill here is celebrated as a form of joy, never mere labor.",
          "paths": [
            "The Market Green",
            "The Inventors' Ateliers",
            "The Great Forge-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Inventors' Ateliers": {
          "description": "A cluttered warren of gnome workshops where the inventors of Dothion tinker at a thousand clever contraptions, from self-turning waterwheels to music-boxes that play a soul's happiest memory. The ateliers are gleeful chaos, every surface heaped with gears, springs, half-finished devices, and inspired nonsense, and the air crackles with the delight of minds forever chasing the next clever idea. It is here that the ambitious young inventors gather, and here that the whispered talk of the sealed deep vaults and their forbidden wonders runs most eagerly among those who chafe at their elders' caution.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guild Row",
            "The Trapdoor Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Farmers' Grain-Halls": {
          "description": "The great storehouses and trading-halls where the harvest of Dothion's never-failing farms is gathered, measured, and traded. The grain-halls smell of clean straw and ripe abundance, and the halfling farmers who fill them take deep pride in the fruits of their honest labor. Here the produce that feeds all of Dothion — and much that is carried to the tables of the higher paradises — is managed with cheerful efficiency, and the farmers gather to trade news, boast of their harvests, and plan the shared work of the fields.",
          "paths": [
            "The Market Green",
            "The Brewing Quarter",
            "The Shrine of Yondalla"
          ]
        },
        "The Trapdoor Hall": {
          "description": "A great hall on the edge of the Market Green whose floor is a massive trapdoor opening onto the topmost entrance of the deep gnome tunnels that honeycomb the earth beneath Dothion. Gnomes come and go between the sunlit surface and the glittering underworld below, hauling up gems and clever wares and hauling down supplies. The hall is the gateway between Dothion's two worlds — the tidy farms above and the ancient tunnel-realm beneath — and the Keepers of the Deep maintain a quiet watch here over who descends and what they seek.",
          "paths": [
            "The Market Green",
            "The Inventors' Ateliers",
            "The Upper Tunnels"
          ]
        },
        "The Great Forge-Hall": {
          "description": "The largest smithy in Glitterhearth, where master smiths work good metal into fine tools, and where the warm forge-glow that gives the town its name lights the evenings. The forge-hall is a place of honest heat and ringing hammers, and its masters are famed for tools that never dull and locks that never fail. Petitioner smiths from across Dothion come to learn here, and the hall's great central forge is said to have been blessed by Garl Glittergold himself, so that nothing wrought in true good faith upon it can ever be turned to cruel purpose.",
          "paths": [
            "The Guild Row",
            "The Shrine of Garl Glittergold"
          ]
        },
        "The Brewing Quarter": {
          "description": "A fragrant district of breweries, bake-houses, and kitchens where the food and drink that make Dothion's tables so joyful are made. The quarter smells of hops, fresh bread, and roasting feasts, and its brewers and bakers are among the most beloved folk in Glitterhearth, for they provide the good cheer that crowns every gathering. Halfling family recipes passed down through petitioner-generations are perfected here, and the quarter's ale-halls are warm, loud, and always full of song.",
          "paths": [
            "The Farmers' Grain-Halls",
            "The Welcoming Inns"
          ]
        },
        "The Welcoming Inns": {
          "description": "A cluster of snug halfling-run inns where travelers, traders, and pilgrims find warm beds, hot meals, and famously generous hospitality. The inns of Glitterhearth are a byword across Dothion for comfort and welcome, their hearths always lit and their tables always laden, and no weary traveler is ever turned away. The innkeepers know all the news and gossip of the cultivated paradise, and their common-rooms are the best place in town to hear of happenings from every village and to arrange passage to wherever one wishes to go.",
          "paths": [
            "The Market Green",
            "The Brewing Quarter"
          ]
        },
        "The Shrine of Garl Glittergold": {
          "description": "A cheerful shrine to Garl Glittergold, the gnomish god of humor, invention, and protection, decorated with clever mechanisms, hidden jokes, and glittering gems. The shrine honors the god's threefold nature — the joy of a good laugh, the delight of a clever making, and the fierce protection of home and folk — and its petitioner-keepers are as quick with a prank as with a prayer. Gnomes come here to bless their inventions and to seek the god's protection, and the shrine holds the town's memory of Garl's greatest trick: the defeat of a great evil through wit rather than force.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Forge-Hall"
          ]
        },
        "The Shrine of Yondalla": {
          "description": "A warm, homely shrine to Yondalla, the halfling goddess of hearth, family, and the harvest, its altar a simple hearthstone always kept warm and its walls hung with the tokens of countless families. The shrine honors the goddess who watches over home, kin, and the shared table, and halfling families come here to bless new homes, new children, and new harvests. It is one of the most beloved places in Glitterhearth, radiating the deep, simple goodness of hearth and home that lies at the heart of all Dothion.",
          "paths": [
            "The Farmers' Grain-Halls"
          ]
        },
        "The Upper Tunnels": {
          "description": "The topmost galleries of the vast gnome tunnel-network, glittering caverns of worked stone lit by gnomish gems where the surface town meets the ancient underworld below. The upper tunnels are busy and safe, full of workshops, storehouses, and the clatter of industrious gnomes, but they are only the beginning: from here passages wind down into deeper, older, stranger reaches, toward the sealed vaults and their forbidden wonders, and toward the whispered places where the tunnels wander too far down. The Keepers of the Deep watch the ways that lead below.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trapdoor Hall",
            "The Descent to the Deep Vaults"
          ]
        },
        "The Descent to the Deep Vaults": {
