    "Wardenmeet": {
      "name": "Wardenmeet",
      "basicInfo": "The great gathering-ground at the heart of Shurrock, a sacred clearing where the free folk of the wild, the Wardens, and the noble beast-spirits meet beneath the open sky to share news, trade, feast, honor the wilderness, and settle what few disputes arise among the wild-hearted. Wardenmeet is not a town — Shurrock has no towns — but a place, an ancient meeting-ground in a vast forest clearing ringed by towering old-growth trees and watched over by a circle of standing stones older than memory. It is the one place in trackless Shurrock where the scattered free folk reliably come together, and thus it samples the whole of the wild paradise in a single gathering: here one finds the roving Wardens of the Wild and their guardian-lore, the free rangers and hunters with news from every corner of the forest, the herders and wanderers, the sacred-grove keepers, and the noble beast-spirits — great stags and bears and wolves and eagles wiser than any mortal beast — all mingling in the easy fellowship of those who love the free wild. Wardenmeet is where a visitor to Shurrock should come first, for from here the trails lead to every forest, peak, river, valley, and sacred grove in the wild world, and here the wandering folk who know those trails may be found and asked. It is a place of open sky, shared fires, told tales, honored spirits, and the deep, patient watchfulness of those who guard a paradise without walls. It rises toward the mountain-passes at the plane's center where a traveler may cross over into cultivated Dothion hanging in the opposite sky.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 7,
      "region": "Shurrock",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Great Clearing": {
          "description": "The wide central meadow of Wardenmeet, ringed by towering ancient trees, where the free folk of Shurrock gather beneath the open sky to meet, feast, and share the news of the wild. The clearing is dotted with shared fire-circles and simple shelters, and it fills with wanderers, Wardens, and beast-spirits when the meets are called. Unlike any place in tidy Dothion, it has no buildings of ambition, no fences, no permanent structures — only the open ground, the great trees, the sky, and the easy fellowship of the wild-hearted. It is the beating heart of free Shurrock.",
          "paths": [
            "The Circle of Standing Stones",
            "The Wardens' Fire",
            "The Trading Glade",
            "The Trailheads"
          ]
        },
        "The Circle of Standing Stones": {
          "description": "An ancient ring of weathered standing stones at the edge of the Great Clearing, older than any memory, where the free folk honor the spirits of the wild and hold their most solemn gatherings. The stones are said to have stood since Bytopia's youth, and the beast-spirits treat them with deep reverence. Here the unwritten code of Shurrock — that the strong shield the weak, that the wild be kept free and pure — is renewed and spoken aloud, and here the gravest matters of the wild are decided by those who gather in the ancient ring.",
          "paths": [
            "The Great Clearing",
            "The Sacred Grove"
          ]
        },
        "The Wardens' Fire": {
          "description": "A great fire-circle where the Wardens of the Wild gather between their roving patrols to share what they have seen in the trackless forests and to coordinate their lonely vigil over Shurrock's freedom and purity. The Wardens are grave, watchful guardians, and their fire is a place of serious counsel amid the general merriment of the meet. It is here that the eldest Warden has begun to voice her fears of a corruption taking root in the deep forests, and here that the Wardens plan their search for a shadow they can feel but cannot yet find.",
          "paths": [
