        "The Wanderers' Camp": {
          "description": "A loose scatter of temporary camps where the wandering folk of Shurrock rest during the meets before returning to their roaming lives. The camp is a cheerful, transient place of shared fires and told tales, where rangers, hunters, herders, and wayfarers from across the wild trade the stories of their travels. Nothing here is permanent, for the wanderers prize their freedom to move on, but while they gather, the camp is warm with the fellowship of kindred free spirits and rich with news from every corner of the wild.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trading Glade"
          ]
        },
        "The River Landing": {
          "description": "A landing on the clean, rushing river that runs past Wardenmeet, where those who travel the wild by water put in to join the meet. The river is one of Shurrock's great highways, running clear and cold over bright stones, and the folk who ply it in light craft bring news and goods from far downstream. The landing is a good place to hear of happenings in the river-valleys and to arrange passage along the water into parts of the wild the land-trails do not easily reach.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trailheads"
          ]
        },
        "The Mountain Path": {
          "description": "The trail that climbs from Wardenmeet toward the soaring peaks at the plane's center, rising toward the high boundary where a traveler may cross over into cultivated Dothion hanging in the opposite sky. The path leads up through ever-wilder country toward the shared band of light where the gravity of one layer gives way to the other, and hardy wanderers take it to make the great crossing between the Twin Paradises. It is the wild world's road to its cultivated twin, and the Wardens watch it, for the crossing is a point where troubles might pass between the layers.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trailheads"
          ]
        },
        "The Deep Forest Verge": {
          "description": "The edge of the vast, ancient old-growth forest that stretches away from Wardenmeet into the trackless heart of Shurrock, where the trees grow oldest and the wild runs deepest. The verge is the threshold of the true wilderness, and beyond it lie forests so deep and old that even the Wardens do not know all their secrets. It is somewhere in these deep woods that the eldest Warden believes the corruption has taken root, and the verge is where the search parties set out into the green immensity, seeking the shadow at the heart of the wild.",
          "paths": [
            "The Trailheads"
          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
