      "difficultyTier": "2",
      "hiddenInfo": "The unease of the beast-spirits at Wardenmeet has a specific source that the eldest Warden has not yet confirmed but deeply fears: a spring deep in the old-growth forest beyond the Deep Forest Verge has been subtly poisoned, and the corruption is spreading downstream through the interconnected waters of the wild, tainting the roots of the trees and the instincts of the beasts that drink. Worse, the fiendish agent responsible did not come from outside — it crept up into Shurrock through one of the deep gnome tunnels that wander too far down from Dothion and open, far below, onto the wild layer's roots. The corruption of the wild and the digging beneath the cultivated world are thus already secretly connected: a single patient fiend, working both weak points at once, seeks to poison Shurrock's nature while whispering the ambitious young gnomes toward the Bridging Engine, so that when the two layers are joined, the rot in the wild will have the whole of the Twin Paradises to spread through. The Wardens and the Keepers of the Deep have never compared notes, and neither yet knows the other faces the same enemy.",
      "known": true
    },
