      "basicInfo": "The great island-hermitage and contemplative shore at the heart of Thalasia, where the deeply fulfilled souls and the wise sea-guardinals dwell in profound peace beside the vast still sea, and where the deepest mysteries of Elysium are quietly kept. Stillmere is a scatter of serene islands and gentle shores wrapped in the dreamlike silver-blue stillness of the deep-sea layer, the calm at the very bottom of Elysium's long descent. It samples the whole of Thalasia: the island-hermitages where contemplative souls reflect, the quiet shores of deep peace, the deep-sea sanctuaries of the sea-guardinals, and — out across the still water — the great heart of the sea where the River Oceanus completes its journey and where the passage beyond is said to lie. From Stillmere the calm waters open toward every island and depth in the layer. Here the good that has come fully to rest dwells in serene contemplation, and here, near the stillest water, lie both the plane's deepest mystery and its most vulnerable secret. It is a place of profound quiet, dreamlike light, and the peace of a long journey nearing its fulfilled end.",
