      "difficultyTier": "4",
      "hiddenInfo": "Some of Mithardir's dead gods are not gone but merely sleeping, faded almost to nothing yet not extinguished — reservoirs of divine power lying unguarded in the dust — and the enemy's whole design is to send a flood of corrupted emotion cascading down from Arvandor and Aquallor to wake one. A forgotten god roused not by worship but by a tide of obsession and despair would rise mad, its divinity rekindled by corruption rather than love, a god of ruin born from the ash of a god that was — a weapon that could shatter all Arborea. The corrupted tide is being steered toward the Avoided Tomb, the greatest sleeper, its name forgotten even by the keepers; the Seeping Sands show the taint already arriving, and the Stirring Dunes show the sleeper beginning to wake. The ancient mystic has grasped the truth — that the passion burning wrong above is being funneled down toward the one grave that must never be disturbed — but whether the gods of Arvandor can be roused to see the danger in time is the question on which all Arborea turns.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Great Mead-Hall": {
      "name": "The Great Mead-Hall",
      "basicInfo": "The roaring gathering-hall at the heart of Ysgard's first layer, greatest of the mead-halls of the slain, standing upon a mighty earthberg where the hero-souls feast, fight, and are chosen by the valkyries, and where the eternal glorious struggle of the plane has its beating heart. The Great Mead-Hall is no city but a vast complex of feast-halls, battle-plains, and earthberg-wilds gathered around the mightiest hall of the fallen, a place of thunderous song and clashing arms open to the golden sky. It samples the whole first layer: the roaring feast-hall of the heroes, the eternal battle-plain of glorious daily war, the valkyries' aerie, the high seat of the gods, and the drifting earthberg-edge where adventure waits over the drop. From here the floating lands open in every direction across the endless sky. It is the most gloriously alive place in the plane — feast, battle, boast, and song at full roar — and the place where the sacred cycle of death and rebirth has begun, terribly, to fail.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 6,
      "region": "Ysgard",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Feast-Hall": {
          "description": "A roaring hall where the fallen heroes feast on endless mead and roast, boasting of deeds and breaking into friendly brawls beneath ancient rafters hung with trophies.",
          "paths": [
            "The Battle-Plain",
            "The Valkyries' Aerie"
          ]
        },
        "The Battle-Plain": {
          "description": "The wide plain where the hero-souls die each day in glorious combat and rise whole each dawn — the eternal joyous war at the heart of the plane's goodness.",
          "paths": [
