          ]
        }
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Aesir and Vanir",
        "The Valkyries",
        "Hero-souls of the mead-halls",
        "The einherjar",
        "Wild spirits of the hunt"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "2",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Fallen Field is the visible wound in Ysgard's sacred cycle: warriors who fall now sometimes stay truly, finally dead, their glorious rebirth denied, and the joy of the eternal struggle curdles into real grief. An unseen enemy means not to conquer the drifting lands but to break the rebirth-cycle itself, turning glorious war into glorious slaughter — for Ysgard's whole goodness rests on the promise that bold death is not final here. The valkyries have felt the wrongness first and traced it to the Fireward Drop, where the corruption rises from the earthberg's fire toward Muspelheim below. Worst of all, the Norse gods live under the shadow of Ragnarok, and a corruption that makes death permanent threatens to turn that distant myth into immediate catastrophe — for gods who cannot be reborn are gods who can be ended.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Molten Forge-Hold": {
      "name": "The Molten Forge-Hold",
      "basicInfo": "The great blazing fortress-forge at the heart of Muspelheim, where the fire giants labor and war amid rivers of molten rock, and where the fierce fire of Ysgard's second layer runs at its hottest — the flame-heart of the plane. The Molten Forge-Hold is no city but a mighty complex of volcanic foundries, fire-plains, ember-wastes, and molten rivers gathered around the fire giants' greatest forge, a place of roaring flame and ringing hammers beneath a smoke-red sky. It samples the whole fire-realm: the fire giants' blazing forge-halls, the molten rivers and fire-seas, the volcanic peaks, the ember-wastes of the fiercest trials, and — deepest of all — the Primordial Forge from which all the layer's flame flows. From here the burning land stretches to a shimmering horizon. It is a harsh, glorious, dangerous place where only the strong endure, and the true battleground of the corruption that seeks to turn the sacred fire of rebirth into a fire of final death.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "radius": 6,
      "region": "Muspelheim",
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "areas": {
        "The Fire Giants' Forge": {
          "description": "A blazing foundry where the fire giants forge mighty works and test their strength, the ring of hammers and roar of flame echoing across the burning land.",
          "paths": [
