      "factions": [
        "The fire giants of the flame-forges",
        "Fire spirits and salamanders",
        "The Smiths of the Molten Forge",
        "Fierce warrior-souls of the heat"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "3",
      "hiddenInfo": "Muspelheim's fire is the deep source of the rebirth-magic that lets Ysgard's fallen rise again — the flame on every earthberg's underside kindled from here — which makes the fire-realm the true battleground of the corruption. The Cold-Flame Reach shows it: molten rivers burning cold and wrong, giving nothing back, so warrior-souls who fall near them do not rise. The enemy's target is the Primordial Forge, the source-fire older than the Norse gods; to corrupt it would turn every flame in Ysgard into a fire of final death, breaking the plane's promise at its root and dooming even its gods. The ancient smith-keeper has felt the wrongness creeping toward the source and suspects the enemy comes not from the fire at all but from the deep dark of Nidavellir below, using Muspelheim's flame as the instrument of a design aimed at all three layers.",
      "known": true
    },
    "The Deep Forge-Hold": {
      "name": "The Deep Forge-Hold",
      "basicInfo": "The great dwarf-hold at the heart of Nidavellir, hewn from the living stone of the deep dark, where the master-smith dwarves delve and forge their legendary works in the ringing, glowing underworld beneath the burning and floating realms above. The Deep Forge-Hold is the one true settlement-form in all of Ysgard — a stone city carved into the deep rock, its halls ringing with hammers and lit by forge-fire and molten metal — and it samples the whole deep-dark layer: the great dwarf-hold carved in stone, the ringing forge-halls of legendary craft, the glittering mines and ore-veins, the rivers of molten metal, and the deepest shunned caverns where old and secret things abide. From here the endless caverns and mines open in every direction through the glowing dark. It is a layer of craft, endurance, and deep patient strength — and the hidden origin of the whole design against Ysgard, for the enemy crept up from these deepest caverns, and the dwarves' tampered forges are the true, unrecognized front line of the war.",
