        "Dwarf-souls of craft and stone",
        "The keepers of the oldest caverns",
        "Deep spirits of metal and rock"
      ],
      "difficultyTier": "4",
      "hiddenInfo": "The enemy breaking Ysgard's rebirth-cycle did not come from fire or the floating lands but crept up from Nidavellir's deepest, most forgotten caverns — the Shunned Deep — choosing to work through fire and craft rather than open battle, precisely because Ysgard's warriors know how to answer a charge but not a poison seeping up from below. The dwarves have grasped part of it: the Tampered Anvil shows sacred implements of the rebirth-magic corrupted at the forge, so that what should preserve life now ends it. The enemy's prize is the Sundering Vein, an ore that unmakes rather than builds and can sever the cords of rebirth; worked into Muspelheim's Primordial Forge above, it would turn the whole plane's sacred fire into a fire of final death. The eldest smith has sealed the way to the Vein, but corrupted forges and turned dwarf-souls mean the seals may not hold — and the dwarves alone have the craft-knowledge to see that their quiet deep forges are the true front line of a war the roaring heroes above do not yet know they are losing.",
      "known": true
