      "name": "In the Thick of It",
      "description": "You are already on a job, deep in hostile territory, and things are about to get complicated. The nature of this mission and/or contract will be directly derived from backstory and or fully.",
      "storyStart": "Drop the player right into the middle of a tense, ongoing contract or mission derived directly from their backstory. They are deep in a dungeon, a treacherous forest, or a hostile urban alleyway. Describe the immediate environment: dripping stalactites, overgrown ancient ruins, or the stench of a sewer. Establish what they are trying to achieve—stealing an artifact, rescuing a captive, or tracking a beast. Then, introduce a sudden complication. The floor gives way, the target reveals a secondary trap, or a rival adventuring party steps out of the shadows to claim the prize, countless potential complications, be creative. Do not resolve the situation; end the prompt right as the adrenaline spikes and the player must make a split-second decision.",
