    "Washed Ashore": {
      "name": "Washed Ashore",
      "description": "The storm was unnatural. The ship is splinters. You are alive, but stranded on an unfamiliar coast with the tide rising.",
      "storyStart": "Begin with the visceral sensation of waking up on a harsh, sandy beach, coughing up seawater. The player is a survivor of a brutal shipwreck. Describe the wreckage scattered along the shoreline: shattered timber, torn sails, and the occasional lifeless body of a crewmate. The sky is the color of a bruised plum, the storm having just passed. Based on their backstory, establish why they were on the ship in the first place. As the player pulls themselves to their feet, they realize they are not alone on the beach. Something—scavenging sahuagin, opportunistic goblins, or a massive, hungry beast from the nearby jungle—is picking through the wreckage and has just noticed the player moving. They have no time to rest; they must act with whatever detritus they can grab.",
