    "The Fine Art of Murder (Bhaalspawn start)": {
      "name": "The Fine Art of Murder (Bhaalspawn start)",
      "description": "You snapped. You've felt this itching, this pressure behind the eyes, this urge to take a life, something so often frowned upon. The sun rose to screams as you took a life in haste. You expected to rot in a cell forever, just another stain on the long history of the city of Baldur's Gate, but a strange, short, wrinkly figure in a tophat has other plans.",
      "storyStart": "Begin with a story start of the player in Wyrm's Rock dungeon. They're sitting, somewhat serene, awaiting their sentencing. Describe the past week or so, as the player was afflicted with a strange itch, a pressure behind the eyes, an insatiable urge to do *something* that the player did not identify until they stumbled upon a murder being investigated by the Flaming Fist. The player was enchanted by the macabre scene, and that's when it became clear, the urge was for violence. They had tried not to snap and act on it, yet they had, killing someone very brutally, the morning sun rising to the screams of onlookers and quickly followed by the player being put in a cell. But, silver lining, the urge feels distant, satiated for now. As the player sits, they hear a polite voice call them 'master' from just outside the cell. Write a scene of Sceleritas Fel, a fiendish goblin creature with red eyes and black scleras, speaking to the player. Make him incredibly entertaining, a true servant of Bhaal. Polite, well-spoken, quite enthusiastic and even kind in a way, but what he says is much more sinister. He appraises the murder the player committed like a particularly enthusiastic critic, even mentioning the raw, unplanned nature of it as a positive, saying that the player will have plenty of time to refine their murder. He phases through the bars, his body glowing a blood red as he does, and then hands the player a key to their cell, saying that he will visit again soon, and implores the player that, next time the urge strikes, to act on it. His last instructions - seek out the Temple of Bhaal hidden underneath the city.",
