    "A Noblewoman of the Web (Menzoberranzan)": {
      "name": "A Noblewoman of the Web (Menzoberranzan)",
      "description": "You are a daughter of a drow Noble House in Menzoberranzan. You have status, enemies, and ambition in equal measure. The question is not whether your rivals will move against you, but when, and whether you will move first (Note: Start designed for you to be a female Drow.",
      "storyStart": "Begin with the player as a daughter of a mid-tier Noble House of Menzoberranzan, established enough to have enemies but not powerful enough to be untouchable. Open with the player in the receiving chamber of their House, dressed formally, in the middle of a delicate social obligation — receiving a visit from a representative of a more powerful House, or attending a gathering of noble daughters at a neutral location. Establish the texture of drow high society: the exquisite poisoned politeness, the compliments that are threats, the alliances that shift like stalactites. Every word spoken has two meanings and the player must navigate this effortlessly, or appear to. Weave in Lolth's faith as a constant social underpinning — the Matron Mothers, the Priestesses, the weight of religious expectation on every noble woman. Introduce a specific, immediate political problem: a rival House daughter has said something that is technically complimentary but functionally a declaration of intent, a younger sister has done something reckless that could expose the House, or a Priestess has summoned the player privately for reasons not yet stated. The player is powerful within their world, but that world is a knife's edge. End the scene at the moment where the player must make the first move, respond to a provocation, or decide how to read a situation that could go several ways.",
