    "Backstory Focus (Nine Hells)": {
      "name": "Backstory Focus (Nine Hells)",
      "description": "Begin the tale at a moment that is meaningful to who you are. The opening will be drawn directly from what made you the person standing here today (Note: Due to how Voyage's story start system works, story starts place you in a location randomly assigned from a list made by the creator. Meaning this start is going to place you in one of the few places in the Hells where a mortal can stand around without being immediately processed, randomly chosen between the Wandering Emporium, the Iron City of Dis, and Abriymoch).",
      "storyStart": "Generate a story start built directly from the player's backstory. Examine their background, profession, traits, special conditions, and any notable family, factions, or events referenced in their history, then craft an opening that meaningfully reflects those elements within the Nine Hells. Critically, establish WHY a mortal is here at all — a contract, a hunt, a pilgrimage, a job, a debt, a patron's summons, an exile — because the Hells do not receive casual visitors, and the reason must be grounded in their established life. The scene should feel like a natural continuation or consequence of that life rather than a generic adventure hook. Make important note as to why the player is where they are according to their backstory, how the events shape how they behave, and obviously relate the main plot occurring to their backstory. Leave the scene poised on an inflection point where the player must make a decision, but do not predetermine which direction they will choose.",
