    "Backstory Focus - Relaxed Ver. (Nine Hells)": {
      "name": "Backstory Focus - Relaxed Ver. (Nine Hells)",
      "description": "Begin the tale at a moment that is meaningful to who you are, as relaxed as the Nine Hells will allow. The opening will be drawn directly from what made you the person standing here today, but this version will not introduce any major plot hook or immediate threat. (Note: Due to how Voyage's story start system works, story starts place you in a location randomly assigned from a list made by the creator. Meaning this start is going to place you in one of the few places in the Hells where a mortal can stand around without being immediately processed, randomly chosen between the Wandering Emporium, the Iron City of Dis, and Abriymoch).",
      "storyStart": "Generate a story start built directly from the player's backstory. Examine their background, profession, traits, special conditions, and any notable family, factions, or events referenced in their history, then craft an opening that meaningfully reflects those elements within the Nine Hells. Critically, establish WHY a mortal is here at all — a contract, a job, a debt, a patron's arrangement, a long-term residence — because the Hells do not receive casual visitors, and the reason must be grounded in their established life. Make important note as to why the player is where they are according to their backstory and how their history shapes how they carry themselves in this place. Leave the scene poised on an inflection point where the player must make a decision, but do not predetermine which direction they will choose. THIS IS A SLICE OF LIFE START. DO NOT FORCE OR INTRODUCE ANY PLOT HOOKS OR THREATS, KEEP IT SLICE OF LIFE AND ENTERTAINING. The Hells being what they are, ambient menace is fine as texture, but nothing may actually threaten the player or demand their attention.",
