      "description": "Fortune check for WAITING TO SEE A RESULT. Use Circumstance when the player is not personally performing the uncertain deed this turn, and is instead waiting, watching, listening, standing by, passing time, or trying to learn how something turned out.\n\nThe subject is whatever they are waiting on: news, weather, a vote, a wound, a ship, a trial, a rumor, an experiment, someone else's action, a thing they did earlier, a thing they only asked about. Do not assume they sent an agent or authored a plan.\n\nFIRE when the action is about the outcome of something already in motion or already at stake, and the player's move this turn is to wait for that outcome.\n\nDo NOT use Circumstance when they are personally doing the deed in this scene (fighting, talking someone down, sneaking, casting, searching this room, traveling, crafting). Use the skill for that method.\n\nNOT simple: waiting is not a free success if an outcome is at stake. NOT impossible merely because the result is offscreen, happens to other people, or is something they want to see rather than do.\n\nImpossible only if there is nothing to resolve: no subject, empty waiting with no stake, or a result that cannot exist in this world.\n\nDifficulty from how hard that OUTCOME is, not from standing still. Easy = likely to go their way. Medium = ordinary uncertainty. Hard = competent opposition, public stakes, fragile situation. Very Hard / Extremely Hard = the result was always a long shot."
