          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The player's attack goes catastrophically wrong and they suffer a CRITICAL INJURY — a real, lasting wound of your choosing, grounded in the logic of this exact moment. The cause may be direct (a riposte slits their eye; the ogre wrenches their shoulder from its socket) or a freak accident the failed attack set in motion (their wild swing shatters a beam and falling masonry smashes their arm bones). Vary the cause — not always the enemy's counter — but never arbitrary: room, enemy, and failed action should conspire to produce it. Pool: lost eye, ear, nose, teeth, or fingers; a hand or foot crushed or severed; an arm or leg broken, mangled, or taken; cracked ribs, shattered collarbone, torn hamstring, punctured lung, deep burn, skull fracture. Depict it with unflinching weight; it is permanent until properly healed and changes how the player fights. The injury maims; it does not kill. The player stays conscious and the fight continues, worse than it was."
